<<<
GENERIC NAMES AND OTHER ALLUSIVE COMMONPLACES.

When Shylock hailed Portia as A Daniel come to judgement, he was using a generic name in the sense here intended;
===
**GENERIC NAMES AND OTHER ALLUSIVE COMMONPLACES.**

When Shylock hailed Portia as *A Daniel come to judgement,* he was using a generic name in the sense here intended;
>>>

<<<
When we talk of the Mecca of Free Trade, of the Huns, of Ithuriel’s spear, of a Naboth’s vineyard, of shooting Niagara, of Procrustean regulations, draconic severity, or tantalizing opportunities, we are using allusive commonplaces.
===
When we talk of *the Mecca of Free Trade,* of *the Huns,* of *Ithuriel's spear,* of *a Naboth's vineyard,* of *shooting Niagara,* of *Procrustean regulations, draconic severity,* or *tantalizing opportunities,* we are using allusive commonplaces.
>>>
